warning[W0801]: `Drink` binds a new name here — it does not test the variant `Kind.Drink`
 --> mem:///main.lu:4:9
  |
1 | enum Kind { Drink, Food, Gratuity }
  |             ----- `Drink` is declared here, in `Kind`
...
4 |     let Drink @ (k, n) = (Kind.Food, 3)
  |         ^^^^^ a binding, not a test
  |
  = note: a `let`, `var`, `for` or `else |…|` pattern binds every value it meets, so a bare name
    there is a new binding even when it spells a variant. To test the value, `match` on it
    (`Kind.Drink => …`); to keep the binding, give it a lowercase name so it reads as one.
help: bind it under a lowercase name: `drink`
  |
4 |     let drink @ (k, n) = (Kind.Food, 3)
  |
